<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Cavia porcellus Holocene (0 Ma) Turing wavelength at 126.7 µm (tier-5 detail s0) (Cavia porcellus (Guinea pig), I. Enaima (Vertebrata) -> Mammalia (Zootoka) -> Cavia)",
        "Cavia porcellus Holocene (0 Ma) Turing wavelength at 126.7 µm (tier-5 detail s0) faithfully reproduces Cavia porcellus (Guinea pig), I. Enaima (Vertebrata) -> Mammalia (Zootoka) -> Cavia morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Cavia porcellus (Guinea pig), I. Enaima (Vertebrata) -> Mammalia (Zootoka) -> Cavia specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Cavia porcellus (Guinea pig), I. Enaima (Vertebrata) -> Mammalia (Zootoka) -> Cavia" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A published guinea-pig histology plate, a signed nanopublication, or a machine-checked Lean build.",
        "does_not_claim: Sub-bin seed robustness. All four seeds share one radial bin.",
        "does_not_claim: That Pearson r = 1 is an independent time-stepper confirmation. It is the match between the quadratic formula and numpy.linalg.eigvals (RMSE = 0 at roundoff).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Charge sweep m = 1, 2, 3 and seeds 3141-3144 all fall in radial bin k = 0.9856 (lambda = 128.55 µm). The bin width, not a continuous estimator, sets the ensemble CV to 0.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivities scaled so lambda_c = 126.7 µm. sigma(k_c) = 0.3006 > 0 and sigma(0) = -0.3215 < 0.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Gallery segmentation: 110 px = 100 µm, dominant wavelength 78.18 µm, orientation KS 0.077 against the spiral, radial-spectrum cosine 0.987.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Substrate sweep at fixed D: lambda_c(0.20) = 176.95 µm and the homogeneous state restabilizes for b >= 2.5.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg (1979) activator-substrate kinetics and the Swift-Hohenberg (1977) amplitude equation as the normal form of a Turing bifurcation (Cross & Hohenberg 1993).",
        "reported_in_source: Sick et al. (2006) mammalian follicle-spacing reaction-diffusion, the anatomical scale neighbour of this 126.7 µm slot.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) finite-k instability and Murray (1981) coat-pattern wavelength selection.",
        "transfer_boundary: 126.7 µm and age 0 Ma are the slot assignment for the single Holocene Cavia node. Predecessor tier 1267 µm holds exactly 10 s0 waves; successor tier 12.67 µm fits 10 times inside one s0 wave.",
        "transfer_boundary: 78.18 µm on the gallery bar is a property of that image, not a correction to the assigned wavelength." ;
